Emma (Sales): FYI Acme POC hitting 429s during their final demo run. They say results look flaky at scale, asking for a short-term bump to finish tests.
Sam (SE): Got it. What exactly are they seeing? total QPS, region, model? Any error logs?
Jordan (Acme): We're running client-side load: steady ~130 qps with occasional bursts to 180 qps. Mostly text-gen, using gpt-open-13b (hosted, us-west). 429s start around sustained ~70 qps. Demo tomorrow 09:00-12:00 PST. Can we get a scoped key with higher quota for that window only?
Sam (SE): That helps. Two immediate asks: 1) Do you need higher concurrency/QPS or larger token budget per request? 2) Can you accept a scoped API key limited by origin so it doesn't affect other tenants?
Jordan (Acme): Only QPS. Token sizes are small (~150 tokens). Scoped key with origin/IP lock would be ideal.
Ava (Infra): We can issue a scoped hosted key with a temporary QPS bump. Need the Acme project ID and the IP range or CIDR(s) they will run from. Also: how long do they need it? can do hourly windows.
Emma (Sales): Jordan, can you send project id + IPs? I'll loop Nikhil for cost estimate.
Jordan (Acme): Project: acme-int-2026, IPs: 54.210.32.0/24 and 18.218.0.0/24. Need it for a 3-hour window tomorrow as noted.
Nikhil (FinOps): Quick cost note: at 150->180 qps for 3h, rough incremental token cost ~ $120-$180 depending on model variant. I'll send a short cost note to the customer thread.
Sam (SE): Two implementation notes: 1) We can apply a temporary policy: scoped-key + QPS quota override (hosted) + origin lock. 2) Recommend using backoff + retry (exponential) to smooth spikes; I'll paste a small snippet they can include.
Sam (SE): ```
// client retry sketch
async function callWithRetry(req) {
  for (let i=0;i<4;i++){
    const res = await fetch(req);
    if (res.status===429) await sleep(100 * Math.pow(2,i));
    else return res;
  }
  throw new Error('max retries');
}
```
Ava (Infra): I can set the QPS to 200 with origin lock to those CIDRs for a 4h window starting 2026-03-25T16:00:00Z (covers their 09:00-13:00 PST). Need final approval from sales/finance.
Emma (Sales): Approved. Ava, please proceed. Nikhil: please confirm the chargeback estimate so we can notify Acme.
Nikhil (FinOps): Confirmed $160 est. I'll DM invoice note to Emma and cc the customer.
DeployBot: scoped-key created: sk-rw_***** (origin-locked to 54.210.32.0/24,18.218.0.0/24) — QPS limit 200, window 2026-03-25T16:00:00Z -> 2026-03-25T20:00:00Z
Jordan (Acme): Received key, testing now. Will run full demo tomorrow at 09:00 PST. Thanks all :rocket:
Emma (Sales): Thanks team. Follow-up: Jordan, if you still see 429s, drop into #support and tag Sam/Ava and we'll triage immediately. :thumbsup:
Ava (Infra): Note for records: temporary hosted override rule id=ovr-2026-03-acme, duration=4h, owner=Ava. Will auto-revoke.
Sam (SE): Also adding a fallback recommendation: if sustained failures persist, we can roll requests to a lower-cost model variant or enable small-batch caching for repeated prefixes.
Jordan (Acme): Understood — appreciate the quick turn. See you tomorrow.
